# ADR-0001 — Offline First

Status: Accepted
Date: 2026-06-05

## Context

SapiensNote is used where connectivity is limited or absent. The device may go days
without internet. The desktop simulator must also run with no external
dependencies. Capturing an idea must never fail because the network is down.

## Decision

All critical functionality works offline. This includes:

- recording (capture)
- playback
- note and tag management
- local storage (SQLite + filesystem)

Transcription happens off-device, on demand, in the local web dashboard
(see ADR-0004). Its absence never blocks capture.

## Consequences

Positive:
- high availability and a fast, reliable UX
- independence from the cloud for the core loop

Negative:
- merging changes across clients needs delta exchange + last-writer-wins
  (handled by the core's sync client)
